-- title:
--   Coefficientwise Galois action preserves q-integrality
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number, and let $F_N=$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of Laurent series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,j_q$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$, and let $\overline{F}_N=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` be its base change, i.e. the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image of $F_N$ under the coefficientwise embedding of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$. Let $\tau$ be a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$, and let $x\in\overline{F}_N$. The element `arithmeticGalois` $(F_N)(\tau)$ of the group of semilinear automorphisms of $\overline{F}_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the pair consisting of the ring automorphism of $\overline{F}_N$ obtained by applying $\tau$ to each coefficient of a Laurent series (`coeffMap`) together with $\tau$ itself on the base field. The assertion is that this automorphism carries $x$ into the valuation subring `qIntegersBar` of $\overline{F}_N$, namely $\{f : 0\le \mathrm{order}(f)\}$ where the order is that of the underlying Laurent series in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, if and only if $x$ itself lies in that subring.
--
--   This records that the coefficientwise action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ on the base-changed modular function field preserves the valuation subring attached to the $q$-adic place, i.e. the place at the cusp $\infty$ is Galois-stable. It is used in the statements [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois_smul_cuspInftyBar`](thm.html#ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois_smul_cuspInftyBar) and [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois_smul_cuspZeroBar`](thm.html#ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois_smul_cuspZeroBar), which identify the effect of the Galois action on the cusps of the modular curve.
